#!/usr/bin/env -S bashy --bashsharp
~~~skill as guide
---
name: google
description: Google Workspace CLI wrapper for Gmail, Calendar, Tasks, Drive, and self-service BYOP onboarding.
metadata:
  requires: "has=bashy"
---
# Google Workspace CLI (google.bsh)

Agent-friendly Bash# wrapper around the Tier-6 managed external gws (googleworkspace/cli).
Provides self-service Bring-Your-Own-Project (BYOP) onboarding, explicit per-account credential
isolation, secret-in-argv refusal, 25 MiB Drive upload preflight, and composable multi-service
workflows across Gmail, Google Calendar, Google Tasks, and Google Drive.

## Self-Service BYOP Onboarding (Free $0 Google Cloud Project per User)

Because Gmail and Drive use Google Restricted Scopes (which cap unverified shared OAuth clients
at 100 users and share project-level quotas), each user or tenant provisions their own $0 Google
Cloud project:

  bashy google auth-guide account=alice@example.com project=my-bashy-gws
  bashy google auth-setup account=alice@example.com project=my-bashy-gws
  bashy google auth-import ~/Downloads/client_secret.json account=alice@example.com
  bashy google auth-status account=alice@example.com
  bashy google auth-status --vault [account=alice@example.com]
  bashy google auth-export --to-vault account=alice@example.com
  bashy google auth-login account=alice@example.com [scopes=...]   # re-consent, refresh credentials
  bashy google auth-enable-apis account=alice@example.com [project=ID]

Setup, import and login also enable the Drive, Gmail, Calendar and Tasks APIs in
the project (gcloud; the project comes from project= or client_secret.json) and
open Google's consent page in the browser.

Default permissions (scopes=... overrides; short names like drive.file are expanded):
Drive drive.file (only files and folders bashy creates; it can make any folders and
upload into them, but cannot see or change the rest of your Drive), Gmail read,
compose and send (no modify or delete), Calendar events, Tasks. Bare service names
(scopes=gmail,drive) ask gws for its broader per-service scopes.

## Runtime Environment Variables

- GWS_ACCOUNT: Required email address of the active Google account (or pass account=ADDR).
- GWS_CREDENTIALS_FILE: Explicit path to OAuth authorized_user JSON file (optional if imported via auth-import).
- GWS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_FILE: Explicit path to Service Account JSON key file.
- GWS_CONFIG_ROOT: Base directory for per-account credentials (default: ~/.config/bashy/google).
  auth-status checks the local file. Use auth-status --vault to check vault
  presence. auth-export --to-vault stores the local file as
  google/<account>/credentials via standard input.
- GWS_BIN: Override path to the gws executable (default: gws on PATH, else bashy's cached copy).
- GWS_DRIVE_HOME: Default Drive folder name (default: bashy; none = My Drive root).
- GWS_NO_BROWSER: Set to print the consent link instead of opening the browser.
- GWS_GCLOUD_BIN: gcloud used to enable APIs (default: gcloud on PATH; none = skip).

Secrets (token, access_token, refresh_token, client_secret, private_key, password,
api_key, credentials, bearer, authorization) are strictly refused in argv (exit 2,
SECRET_VIA_ARGV).

## Single-Service Verbs

- Gmail: gmail-list, gmail-get, gmail-send, gmail-draft
- Calendar: calendar-list, calendar-get, calendar-create, calendar-update, calendar-delete, calendar-freebusy
- Tasks: tasklists-list, tasks-list, tasks-get, tasks-create, tasks-complete, tasks-update, tasks-delete
  Deletes (calendar-delete, tasks-delete, and raw ... delete/clear/trash) require
  confirm=yes; agents ask the user first.
- Drive: drive-list, drive-search, drive-get, drive-upload, drive-mkdir, drive-home [set id=FOLDER_ID]
  Uploads and new folders go to a "bashy" folder it creates on first use
  (GWS_DRIVE_HOME renames it; GWS_DRIVE_HOME=none means My Drive root) unless parent=FOLDER_ID.
- YouTube: youtube-upload <video-file> title=TEXT [description=TEXT] [privacy=unlisted|private|public] [tags=a,b] [--dry-run]
  Uploads to the channel of the signed-in account (default unlisted) and prints the
  watch URL and the privacy-friendly embed URL to link from an app or site. One-time
  owner steps, named in the error when missing: grant youtube.upload in its own
  credential slot (auth-login account=ADDR slot=youtube scopes=youtube.upload URL; Google
  will not grant it together with Drive) and enable "YouTube Data API v3"
  in the OAuth client's project. gws has no YouTube service, so this verb calls the
  YouTube Data API directly with the account's own OAuth credentials.
- Escape hatch: raw <service> <resource...>

## Composed Multi-Service Workflows

- mail-to-task <message-id> [tasklist=@default] [due=ISO] [notes=TEXT] [title=TEXT] [--dry-run]
- drive-share-mail <local-path> to=ADDR [subject=SUBJ] [body=TEXT] [parent=FOLDER_ID] [--dry-run]
- agenda [calendarId=primary] [tasklist=@default] [q=is:unread] [maxResults:=10]
~~~

set -euo pipefail
export BASHY_HINTS=off

if [[ "${1:-}" == "--help" || "${1:-}" == "-h" || "${1:-}" == "help" || "${1:-}" == "--skill" ]]; then
  inside=false
  while IFS= read -r line; do
    if [[ $line == '~~~skill as guide' ]]; then inside=true; continue; fi
    if [[ $inside == true && $line == '~~~' ]]; then break; fi
    if [[ $inside == true ]]; then printf '%s\n' "$line"; fi
  done < "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}"
  exit 0
fi

